## Contract (raw three.js ESM module)
{{ frame_doc }}
- `{{ asset_file }}` must `export function build{{ asset_name }}(THREE, opts = {}) { ... return group; }`
  where `group` is a `THREE.Group` whose lowest point is at y=0 and whose footprint is centred on
  the origin, sized as stated (the check errors beyond 2.5 × or under 0.4 × the stated size on any
  axis; the zones place it at scale 1, so the stated size is the target). `opts.seed` (number) and
  `opts.variant` (0..n) may vary details deterministically (`mulberry32(seed)` from `../lib/noise.js`
  or a tiny PRNG inside the file — never Math.random).
- Imports: `three`, `three/addons/*`, `../lib/*.js` and your own relative files — no CDN, no other
  package.  Forbidden: `document.*` / `window.*`, fetch or XHR, `Math.random()`, `Date.now()` /
  `performance.now()`, `requestAnimationFrame`, creating a renderer.  The module is imported and
  built in node (no DOM, no WebGL) the moment it is written: anything that needs a browser throws
  there and the asset is reported broken.
- Procedural geometry built in code (any THREE geometry, including a BufferGeometry you fill
  yourself); no loaded files. Every surface carries a material with a real colour.
- Set `group.userData.size = [w, h, d]` to the measured size.  Optional animation hook:
  `group.userData.update = (t, dt) => {...}` (the zone that places you caches it and calls it;
  `userData.tick` is never called by anything).  Amplitudes must be visible after 1.5 s:
  >= 0.10 rad of rotation or >= 0.05 m of travel — not sub-centimetre jitter.
- Triangle budget: at most 15 000 triangles for one instance (measured when the module is
  imported and built); segment counts are yours within it.
{% if library_rows %}
