## DO / DON'T
- DO use the exact size numbers above; the zone builders rely on them.
- DO make it recognisable as the named thing at scene distance; the description decides which
  features that takes and whether it looks new or used.
- DO make `opts.variant` (0..n) change the silhouette, not just the scale, when the plan places
  several copies: the judge reads identical copies; how many variants is the plan's count.
- DO give a repeated natural asset colour room across copies (`opts.hue` / `opts.tint`, or a
  colour varied from `opts.seed`) so twenty copies are not one colour.
- DON'T model a flat plane with a colour where the thing has real thickness (a fence is stalks and
  rails, not a textured quad) — closeups are judged.
- DON'T leave floating pieces: every sub-shape overlaps a neighbour by ≥ 2 mm.
- DON'T write anything outside the listed file(s).
